  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 3 Level 16 Walkthrough: Attic</h1>

    <p>Attic is the sixteenth room of Chapter 3, <i>Murder Dressed in White</i>, and at eight minutes fifty-six it is the longest of the chapter's three utility rooms. It is also the prettiest: a sloped plank ceiling with skylights, a back wall of built-in shelves, a tall window, a mint-green dresser with a drawer left open, a desk with a typewriter, and a white birdcage on the floor with a yellow bird inside it. The level hides its logic in small objects — a clock missing a hand, a four-digit display under a pair of arrows, an octagon plate, a five-by-five shape grid — and then pays off with one of the few complete results cards in the chapter.</p>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt frame by frame at one frame per second. The four-digit display — <b>3549</b> — was read twice, once from the whole frame and once from a crop, and both passes agreed. The results card was also read twice on three separate values: <b>+50</b> coins, <b>Time: 8:43</b> and a <b>300</b> piggy bank. Anything that only ever read one way is listed under "What this page could not verify" instead of being printed as a solution.</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={3} current={16} variant="jump" label="Chapter 3 · Murder Dressed in White" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>Attic is room 16 of 24 in Chapter 3. The number lock reads <b>3549</b> at 4:39. The room ends completely at 8:55: <b>+50</b> coins, <b>Time: 8:43</b>, piggy bank <b>300</b>.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Read the room from the doorway before moving: sloped ceiling above, shelves along the back wall, dresser and desk to the right, birdcage on the floor.</li>
        <li>Pick up the <b>Clock hand</b> at 0:19. The red hexagonal wall clock at 1:39 is where it belongs.</li>
        <li>Check the inventory strip at 2:59 — the letters <b>R N G N D P A O B E C K L</b> are laid over a tile grid below the action buttons.</li>
        <li>Set the four-digit display to <b>3549</b> at 4:39; the up arrow sits above the digits and the down arrow below.</li>
        <li>Work the octagon plate at 4:59, then the five-by-five shape grid at 5:59.</li>
        <li>Finish at the birdcage. At 8:23 the attic is lit and the cage is the last object on screen.</li>
        <li>The results card lands at 8:55: <b>+50</b>, <b>Time: 8:43</b>, piggy <b>300</b>, bank full.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
